 ],
 "synopsis": "Bandhan Bank shares jumped nearly 7% after reports that Abu Dhabi-based International Holding Company (IHC) was in early-stage discussions to acquire a promoter stake in Bandhan Financial Services (BFSL). BFSL has been working with advisers Jefferies to find strategic investors for a 25-32% stake. The potential transaction aims to provide an exit opportunity for early-stage financial investors, including GIC of Singapore and the International Finance Corporation (IFC), whose stake alone could be valued at $500-600 million. Additional entities canvassed for the stake include First Abu Dhabi Bank, Qatar Investment Authority, Carlyle, and EQT.",
